  "id": "Compound::DB00129 - Gene::6542",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which L-ornithine may interact with Slc7a2, through a series of molecular and functional connections. L-ornithine binds to Slc7a3, which is involved in the transport of basic amino acids across cell membranes, and Slc7a3 is also associated with the transport of L-ornithine. This implies that L-ornithine may influence the function of Slc7a2 through a transmembrane transporter pathway, possibly by modulating the activity of Slc7a3. The shared involvement of Slc7a2 in the transport of amino acids suggests that L-ornithine could act as a substrate or regulator of this transporter, potentially affecting cellular uptake or efflux of amino acids. The evidence is supported by the presence of multiple paths linking L-ornithine to Slc7a2 through different transporter activities, indicating a plausible, if not fully elucidated, mechanism of action. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Slc7a2 in amino acid transport and suggests that L-ornithine may exert its effects through a mechanism involving the regulation of this transporter.",
